.TH AGRF 1 "2026-09-02" "agrf" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agrf \- stream of numbers to a braille unicode graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agrf
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIVALUES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agrf
reads whitespace\-separated integers or floats from positional
arguments (if any) or standard input and draws them as a compact
sparkline / bar chart using braille dots (U+2800).
.PP
Each value maps to one pixel column; two columns fit in one braille
character, so a graph
.I W
characters wide shows the last 2*\fIW\fR values, filled left to right.
Non\-numeric tokens become gaps (empty columns). The vertical scale runs
from
.B \-\-min
(default 0) to
.B \-\-max
(default: the window maximum); values outside the range clamp to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " \fIN\fR"
Output width in characters; holds 2*\fIN\fR values. Default: 20.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-height " \fIN\fR"
Output height in characters; 4 pixels per character. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-\-min " \fIF\fR"
Y\-axis minimum; values below are clamped. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max " \fIF\fR"
Y\-axis maximum; values above are clamped. Default: auto (window max).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-point
Point mode: draw only the marker at each value, without filling
underneath. Default: bars.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Plot a sequence across the default width:
.RS
.EX
seq 1 100 | agrf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Ping latency as a sparkline, two rows tall:
.RS
.EX
ping \-c 20 1.1.1.1 | grep \-oP 'time=\eK[0-9.]+' | agrf \-w 20 \-H 2
.EE
.RE
.PP
Positional values in point mode:
.RS
.EX
agrf \-p 3 7 2 9 5
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if standard input cannot be read, and 2 on
invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/rmrfus/agrf
